; 04-no-output-before-eof.l0 -- the nearest program L0 can express to "ask a
; name, then greet it". It is NOT the prompt program: it is the evidence that
; the prompt program cannot be written.
;
; Blocks: prompt; also linefilter and counter as pipeline stages (neither can
; write a result for a line while later input is still to come).
;
; The question is part of main's result, and section 9 writes that result
; only after main returns, and calls main only after standard input has
; reached end of file. So the question can never be on the screen while the
; user could still answer it. prompt/measure.sh times this.

(def main ((input (list int))) (list int)
  (rev (push "!\n"
         (push (take_line input)
           (push "What is your name? Hello, " (nil int))))))
